# Mali section, as tools/cts/mali-deqp-e2e-selftest.sh expects it

The counts below are written by hand for the three fake-board slices the
self-test makes (4 Pass, 1 Fail, 2 Lost of 7 cases); @SHA8@ is replaced by the
commit of the self-test's throwaway repository. They are not read back from
`mali-deqp-tally.py --markdown`.

<!-- mali-deqp-tally begin -->

Slices: `t6-gles2-e2e-clean`, `t6-gles2-e2e-crash`, `t6-gles2-e2e-hang`
(commits `@SHA8@`).

| Status | Cases |
| --- | ---: |
| Pass | 4 |
| Fail | 1 |
| Lost | 2 |
| **Total** | **7** |

| Status | Cause | Cases |
| --- | --- | ---: |
| Fail | Image comparison failed on <host> at <addr> & <mac> | 1 |
| Lost | chunk-crash | 1 |
| Lost | chunk-hang | 1 |

